# Security Review Standards

## Purpose

Defines criteria for reviewing security of artifacts.

## Review Triggers

- New feature implementation
- New API endpoint
- Authentication/authorization changes
- New dependency
- Infrastructure changes
- Pre-release review

## Review Criteria

### Authentication

- [ ] Authentication mechanism defined
- [ ] Passwords stored securely (hashed + salted)
- [ ] Session management secure
- [ ] Token expiration and refresh handled
- [ ] MFA available for privileged actions
- [ ] Brute force protection in place

### Authorization

- [ ] Least privilege principle applied
- [ ] Role-based access control defined
- [ ] Permission checks at every level
- [ ] No missing authorization on endpoints
- [ ] No default-allow configuration

### Input Validation

- [ ] All inputs validated
- [ ] SQL injection prevention
- [ ] XSS prevention
- [ ] CSRF protection
- [ ] Command injection prevention
- [ ] File upload validation
- [ ] Request size limits

### Data Protection

- [ ] Sensitive data encrypted at rest
- [ ] Data encrypted in transit (TLS)
- [ ] Secrets not in code or config
- [ ] Secrets in secure vault
- [ ] PII handling compliant
- [ ] Data retention defined

### Dependencies

- [ ] No known vulnerabilities
- [ ] Dependencies audited
- [ ] Versions up to date
- [ ] Unused dependencies removed
- [ ] License compliance checked

### Infrastructure

- [ ] Network segmentation
- [ ] Firewall rules configured
- [ ] Least privilege on cloud IAM
- [ ] Logging and monitoring enabled
- [ ] Backup and recovery tested
- [ ] No default credentials

### Code Review

- [ ] No hardcoded secrets
- [ ] No debug endpoints in production
- [ ] No insecure functions used
- [ ] Proper error handling (no info leaks)
- [ ] Security comments addressed

## Common Vulnerabilities Checklist

### OWASP Top 10

- [ ] A01: Broken Access Control
- [ ] A02: Cryptographic Failures
- [ ] A03: Injection
- [ ] A04: Insecure Design
- [ ] A05: Security Misconfiguration
- [ ] A06: Vulnerable and Outdated Components
- [ ] A07: Identification and Authentication Failures
- [ ] A08: Software and Data Integrity Failures
- [ ] A09: Security Logging and Monitoring Failures
- [ ] A10: Server-Side Request Forgery

## Approval Criteria

Security is approved when:

- [ ] No critical vulnerabilities
- [ ] All high findings addressed
- [ ] OWASP Top 10 checklist passed
- [ ] No secrets exposed
- [ ] Dependency audit passed
- [ ] Security review documented
```

