# Documentation Review Standards

## Purpose

Defines criteria for reviewing documentation quality.

## Review Triggers

- New documentation
- Documentation updates
- Feature documentation
- Release documentation
- Pre-release review

## Review Criteria

### Completeness

- [ ] All required sections present
- [ ] All features documented
- [ ] All APIs documented
- [ ] All configuration documented
- [ ] YAML front matter complete

### Accuracy

- [ ] Information is correct
- [ ] Code examples work
- [ ] Commands are correct
- [ ] URLs are valid
- [ ] Screenshots up to date

### Clarity

- [ ] Clear language
- [ ] Logical structure
- [ ] Good headings
- [ ] Terminology defined
- [ ] Examples included

### Consistency

- [ ] Consistent terminology
- [ ] Consistent formatting
- [ ] Consistent style
- [ ] Consistent structure

### Traceability

- [ ] Cross-references valid
- [ ] Related documents linked
- [ ] Version information present
- [ ] Owner identified

### Maintenance

- [ ] Easy to update
- [ ] No duplication (references instead)
- [ ] Clear ownership
- [ ] Version controlled

## Approval Criteria

Documentation is approved when:

- [ ] No missing sections
- [ ] All links valid
- [ ] All examples work
- [ ] Terminology consistent
- [ ] YAML front matter complete
- [ ] Ready for publication
```

